{"created": "2026-10-05T15:10:45.145455+00:00", "modified": "2026-10-05T15:37:44.508521+00:00", "id": 23165736, "conceptrecid": "23164301", "doi": "10.5281/zenodo.23165736", "conceptdoi": "10.5281/zenodo.23164301", "doi_url": "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.23165736", "metadata": {"title": "For every fixed c, s(k^2-c) = k for all large k, with an explicit constant (preprint)", "doi": "10.5281/zenodo.23165736", "publication_date": "2026-10-05", "description": "Licences in this single record: the preprint (paper/paper.pdf, paper/paper.tex) is licensed under CC BY 4.0; the programs and data (code/, data/) under the MIT License, which is the licence shown for the record. Preprint with verification programs. For every fixed c, s(k^2-c) = k for all sufficiently large k, where s(n) is the side of the smallest square containing n non-overlapping unit squares. Explicitly: every packing of N unit squares in [0,k]^2 that are pairwise disjoint as closed sets has k^2 - N &gt;= 0.033 log k for every integer k &gt;= 2 (0.027 log k without the computer-assisted Lemma 4.10). Lemma 4.10 is a branch-and-bound computation re-verified in Arb ball arithmetic; its programs, data and logs are included. Version 1.1 adds two independent checks that the accepted boxes cover the parameter domain. Use of AI: developed with extensive assistance from Claude (Anthropic), including the proofs, the text, the programs and the computation for Lemma 4.10; the author takes full responsibility. Not peer reviewed.", "access_right": "open", "creators": [{"name": "Ryu, Sungjoon", "affiliation": null}], "keywords": ["square packing", "unit squares", "wasted area", "Roth-Vaughan", "c*(k)"], "related_identifiers": [{"identifier": "https://github.com/squarepacker/k2-minus-c/tree/v1.1", "relation": "isSupplementTo", "resource_type": "software", "scheme": "url"}, {"identifier": "10.5281/zenodo.23165916", "relation": "isSupplementTo", "resource_type": "publication-preprint", "scheme": "doi"}], "version": "1.1", "c